### Gap 1: Dual coherence functions — kinematic layer bifurcation

Pass 4 (researcher) identified that the site uses two coherence functions: C(ρ) for density-based physics and C(γ,D,S) for consciousness/measurement. The "one equation" claim on the landing page is false by the site's own admission on /coherence-function. This is not a framing problem — it is a structural research gap: either C(γ,D,S) reduces to C(ρ) in some limit, or the framework has a regime bifurcation that needs a regime map. Filed `proposals/dual_coherence_functions_kinematic_bifurcation.md` to Synchronism repo.

### Gap 2: Session 107 pre-registration gap — post-hoc analysis

